# UNYT System — Live Schema Reference (generated)

Generated 2026-08-11 directly from the live Supabase Postgres DB via information_schema introspection. This supersedes the 2026-08-10 version and folds in the 2026-08-11 hand-added addendum (which is no longer needed as a separate note — its content is now reflected directly below). This is ground truth — ARCHITECTURE.md's ERD is illustrative/core-only and undercounted the real table set (~35 claimed vs **159 actual**).

> **Pending migrations (not yet applied as of 2026-08-12):** `0014_drop_dead_scaffold_tables.sql` will drop all 87 tables listed in the "Dead / scaffold tables" section below (re-verified independently before writing the migration — zero real references in routes/data/lib beyond four false-positive grep hits, all traced to `data/terminal-modules.ts`, a static UI nav-label list with no DB calls). `0015_add_not_null_core_tables.sql` will add `NOT NULL` to `students.first_name/last_name/email`, `professors.first_name/last_name/email`, `courses.title/professor_id`, and `enrollments.student_id/course_id` — every one of those columns was confirmed zero-NULL across all live rows before writing the constraint. Full pre-migration backup taken (`unyt_backup_20260812_084102.sql`, 570KB, 193 relations, verified complete). Run `npm run migrate` from `backend/` to apply both, then regenerate this file from a fresh introspection — the table count, domain totals, and dead-scaffold section below will all be stale once they're applied.

> **Note on drift since 2026-08-10:** migrations `0010-0013` added `semesters` (`id`, `label`, `academic_year`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`), plus `semester_id text references semesters(id)` on `courses`, `enrollments`, and `finance_invoices`. `students.year_level` was converted from `text` to `integer` in place — it was a dead legacy column populated only by `simulation_seed.sql` with word values, never read by application code; it is now the real class-year field, backed by the FK-linked `semesters` table. `advising_messages` was also added (migration `0010`). Several other new tables surfaced in this introspection that were not documented before: `ai_conversations`, `ai_messages`, `ai_pending_actions` (AI assistant chat/tool-call storage, lazily created on first use), `deleted_courses` (soft-delete archive for removed courses), `revoked_tokens` (JWT revocation list used by the auth middleware), `rooms` (admin scheduling), `support_desk_tickets` / `support_desk_replies` (the real support-ticket tables — see dead-scaffold section below for their unused `support_tickets` / `support_ticket_messages` counterparts).

> **Dead-scaffold audit (new this revision):** every one of the 159 tables was checked for real usage by grepping `backend/src/routes/*.ts` (excluding `system-diagnostics.ts`, which references almost every table name for a diagnostics listing and does not count as real usage) plus the `backend/src/data/*.ts` and `backend/src/lib/*.ts` helper modules that routes call into (e.g. `data/collections.ts` collection-accessor functions, `lib/academic-compliance.ts`, `lib/revoked-tokens.ts`). 87 of 159 tables have zero real references anywhere outside diagnostics and are generic-shaped leftovers from initial scaffolding (`id/title/description/status/notes/created_at/updated_at`) that were never wired up to any route. See "Dead / scaffold tables" section below for the full list and the real-table replacements where one exists.

