## Dead / scaffold tables (zero references outside system-diagnostics.ts)

These 87 tables exist in the live DB (mostly generic `id/title/description/status/notes/created_at/updated_at` scaffold shape) but have **zero** references in `backend/src/routes/*.ts` (excluding `system-diagnostics.ts`) or in the `backend/src/data/*.ts` / `backend/src/lib/*.ts` helper modules those routes call into. They are not used by any real application code path — treat them as scaffolding left over from early schema generation, not as a live data model. Do not build new features against these without first wiring up real read/write paths.

Known dead-vs-real duplicate pairs (the dead one is listed first):

| Dead (unused) | Real (actually used) | Used in |
|---|---|---|
| `academic_terms` | `semesters` | `backend/src/lib/academic-terms.ts`, `enrollments.ts` |
| `installment_plans` | `finance_installment_plans` | `backend/src/routes/finance.ts` |
| `books`, `book_copies`, `book_loans`, `book_reservations`, `library_fines` | `library_books`, `library_loans` | `backend/src/routes/library.ts` |
| `interviews` | `interview_schedules` (real, via `interviewSchedulesCollection()`) | `backend/src/routes/admissions.ts` |
| `refund_requests` | `finance_refund_requests` | `backend/src/routes/finance.ts` |
| `support_tickets`, `support_ticket_messages` | `support_desk_tickets`, `support_desk_replies` | `backend/src/routes/support-tickets.ts` |
| `maintenance_mode` | `maintenance_state` (via `maintenanceStateCollection()`) | `backend/src/routes/it-admin.ts` |
| `registration_state` | enrollment-open columns live on `academic_structure`/`courses` instead | `backend/src/routes/enrollments.ts` |
| `departments`, `campuses`, `classes`, `classrooms` | free-text `department`/`campus_id` columns on `students`/`professors`/`courses` | (no dedicated reference-table lookup exists) |

`student_profiles_extra` (pk: `student_id`) is also dead: it duplicated `year_level`, `advisor_id`, `scholarship_status`, `payment_status`, `registration_hold`, `tuition_balance` — all of which now live directly as real columns on `students` (see `students.year_level`, now `integer` and FK-adjacent to `semesters` via `enrollments.semester_id`/`courses.semester_id`). No route reads or writes `student_profiles_extra`.

Full list of the 87 dead/scaffold tables:

`academic_terms`, `accreditation_reports`, `admissions_scholarships`, `advisor_meetings`, `advisor_notes`, `advisor_risk_alerts`, `advisor_student_assignments`, `api_clients`, `application_documents`, `applications`, `assignment_submissions`, `attendance_records`, `attendance_sessions`, `backup_jobs`, `backup_snapshots`, `book_copies`, `book_loans`, `book_reservations`, `books`, `branding_settings`, `campuses`, `classes`, `classroom_schedules`, `classrooms`, `club_memberships`, `clubs`, `course_approval_requests`, `course_materials`, `department_comparisons`, `department_reports`, `departments`, `discipline_cases`, `ebooks`, `email_sms_configs`, `employee_leave_requests`, `entrance_exam_results`, `event_registrations`, `events`, `exam_timetables`, `faculty_budget_requests`, `fee_invoice_items`, `fee_invoices`, `financial_reports`, `global_announcements`, `gradebook_entries`, `graduation_eligibility_checks`, `homework_grading_tasks`, `installment_payments`, `installment_plans`, `interviews`, `journals`, `lab_materials`, `late_penalties`, `leave_requests`, `library_fines`, `login_devices`, `maintenance_mode`, `maintenance_windows`, `multilingual_strings`, `password_reset_audit`, `payroll_items`, `payroll_runs`, `quiz_attempt_answers`, `quiz_attempts`, `quiz_questions`, `refund_requests`, `registration_state`, `research_database_access`, `role_permissions`, `security_incidents`, `security_logs`, `sponsorships`, `sso_providers`, `staff_contracts`, `staff_performance_reviews`, `student_documents`, `student_profiles_extra`, `student_record_changes`, `student_scholarships`, `support_ticket_messages`, `support_tickets`, `system_settings`, `ta_student_support_sessions`, `teaching_assistant_assignments`, `teaching_loads`, `user_role_history`, `welfare_requests`

